# EnvironmentPostProcessors must be registered here (spring.factories), NOT in
# an `org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor.imports` file.
# Spring Boot's EnvironmentPostProcessorApplicationListener loads EPPs only via
# EnvironmentPostProcessorsFactory.fromSpringFactories(), which reads
# META-INF/spring.factories. The `.imports` mechanism is for AutoConfiguration
# only — an EPP listed there is silently never run at boot.
org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
com.nubeero.cia.common.config.PiiKeyValidator,\
com.nubeero.cia.common.config.ProductionSafetyValidator
